Why this file exists, and why it does not say more
--------------------------------------------------

A repository with no licence file is already "all rights reserved" — that is
what copyright does by default. This file changes nothing legally; it removes
the ambiguity, so nobody has to guess whether the absence was a decision or an
oversight. Here it was an oversight, and this is the correction.

The distribution terms are deliberately still open, because that choice runs
one way only: a permission granted publicly cannot be withdrawn from anyone who
already has the code, while a reservation can be relaxed at any time. Reserving
now costs nothing and keeps every option; granting now closes most of them for
good.

This becomes PolyForm Small Business 1.0.0 when the engine is handed to
anybody. That is settled; see README.md.

The engine's own posture on this is in README.md, under "Building it as if it
were licensable": build to a standard that would survive being licensed, and
revisit the terms when a title has actually shipped on it and a second platform
exists. Until then this file stands.

